  <Properties>
    <mainContent>
      <Value><![CDATA[{
  "contentData": [
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "7e5b24ac-fc8e-4b56-93b7-9820810ef7d7",
      "key": "9e449610-0ea8-477a-a793-0e9f92ad6950",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "text",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": {
            "blocks": {
              "contentData": [],
              "settingsData": [],
              "expose": [],
              "layout": {}
            },
            "markup": "\u003Ch2\u003EThe great pause\u003C/h2\u003E\u003Cp\u003EYou pour a little water over fresh grounds, and the whole bed puffs up like a small brown soufflé. Then you wait. Thirty seconds is the usual advice, and Perry has timed enough of them to confirm that it is the longest half-minute of the day, second only to the one before the microwave beeps.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe bloom is carbon dioxide leaving the beans. Fresh coffee holds a lot of it, and if you pour all your water at once, the gas pushes back and the water takes odd little shortcuts. Letting the gas out first gives the rest of the brew a fair chance at an even extraction.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Ch3\u003EWhat to do with your hands\u003C/h3\u003E\u003Cp\u003EThe honest answer is nothing. Resist the urge to stir, tilt, tap or narrate. Some people hum. Perry watches the surface for bubbles and treats a lively bloom as a small personal compliment, which is unscientific and entirely reliable as a mood booster.\u003C/p\u003E\u003Cp\u003EA flat, sullen bloom means the beans are old, and no technique will fix that. It is a good lesson in humility. You can be as careful as you like, and the coffee will still tell you the truth in thirty seconds or fewer.\u003C/p\u003E"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "contentTypeKey": "8f6abe09-cffc-4fe0-a645-b265fdc8010b",
      "key": "3d1df79d-3f75-456e-a305-a1470b9027e8",
      "values": [
        {
          "alias": "quote",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "I have waited for buses with less patience than I give a wet bed of coffee."
        },
        {
          "alias": "attribution",
          "culture": null,
          "editorAlias": null,
          "segment": null,
          "value": "Thaddeus Quillfeather, amateur brewer"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
